@@ -1,6 +1,27 @@
 Verify resumable Stop preserves an active AUTO program and resumes or
 single-steps it.
 
+This directory holds the shared configuration (test.ini, core_sim.hal,
+tool.tbl), the G-code programs and test-ui.py, which runs one scenario per
+LinuxCNC session (selected by RESUMABLE_STOP_SCENARIO). The runtests tests
+are its subdirectories, which run in parallel under ci/test-sharded.sh:
+
+  g76-stop   G76 Stop and clearance, the G76 cut/retract handoff stress test,
+             fperrev
+  g76-step   G76 Single Step (fresh, after Stop, in flight), exit tapers, and
+             the trapezoidal re-run of fperrev
+  threading  G33, G33.1 and G95 Stop cases, commands queued behind them, and
+             the trapezoidal re-run of g33-chain
+  general    everything else, including the at-speed, dwell, orientation and
+             homing scenarios and the trapezoidal re-runs of ordinary and
+             single-step
+
+Each group lists its scenarios in its "scenarios" file. Its test.sh runs them
+through run-scenarios.sh, which starts each from a fresh LinuxCNC session in a
+private copy of the configuration, so groups never share files LinuxCNC
+writes. Its checkresult (check-result.sh) fails unless every listed scenario
+reported success and the count matches the number given in checkresult.
+
 This regression test exercises the task-level Stop operation directly through
 the Python command API. It checks that an active feed move stops without
 aborting queued AUTO state, that spindle and coolant outputs are disabled
@@ -61,6 +82,12 @@ step. It also starts G76 in normal AUTO_RUN, stops after the first pass with
 later passes already queued, and verifies that each following AUTO_STEP
 reaches exactly one cylindrical or tapered safe approach endpoint, and the
 next AUTO_STEP completes that pass's infeed, thread, and clearance.
+In-flight Single Step coverage arms during an ordinary source block with three
+later motion blocks already queued and during an active G76 cut with later
+passes queued. It verifies that the active block or thread-plus-clearance unit
+finishes normally and motion remains at its boundary until Resume. While the
+step is armed and the active unit is still moving, both task and motion report
+unpaused; they change to paused only when motion reaches the latched boundary.
 Arc blending is enabled for all scenarios, so the exact-clearance assertions
 also prove that a marked G76 retract endpoint is not trimmed by a following
 rapid. The handoff stress case uses a slow synchronized feed and issues Stop at
